From bf377c051f09254e5a6581349f91759430f54399 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lars <lars.barring@smhi.se>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:50:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Take symbol case from NIST names; test exactness against SI
 history

- utils/package.py: restore_symbol_case() now uses NIST's own quantity
  names for the constant, from all releases (nist_quantity_names()),
  instead of the curated name_bipm_en column, which differs from NIST for
  118 of 357 constants. A token occurring in more than one case is left
  unchanged. The generated RDF is unchanged.
- tests: label check compares against NIST names; new test that the
  exactness of c, mu0, eps0, Z0, M_u, M(12C), h, e, k and N_A follows the
  SI definitions in force for each release (independent of NIST's
  formatting and of nist/repackage.py).
- utils/codata_constants.py: the NIST override is marked temporary.
- CHANGELOG: updated accordingly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XHM6qC7Y8rv5syejamGbb9
